   582	    /// Mints `token_id`, transfers it to `to`, and checks for `to`'s
   583	    /// acceptance.
   584	    ///
   585	    /// An additional `data` parameter is forwarded to
   586	    /// [`erc721::IErc721Receiver::on_erc721_received`] to contract recipients.
   587	    ///
   588	    /// # Arguments
   589	    ///
   590	    /// * `&mut self` - Write access to the contract's state.
   591	    /// * `to` - Account of the recipient.
   592	    /// * `token_id` - Token id as a number.
   593	    /// * `data` - Additional data with no specified format, sent in the call to
   594	    ///   [`Erc721::_check_on_erc721_received`].
   595	    ///
   596	    /// # Errors
   597	    ///
   598	    /// * [`erc721::Error::InvalidSender`] - If `token_id` already exists.
   599	    /// * [`erc721::Error::InvalidReceiver`] - If `to` is [`Address::ZERO`], or
